    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d713">

                <pb facs="0730" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">122.352/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-12T11:00:00-05:00">March 12, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>91. Your 189, March 11, 3 p.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d713-f1"/> Department refers
                    to its telegram 23, January 20, 6 p.m.</p>
                <p>Provided the Governments mentioned in Legation’s telegram 97 of January 31, 4
                    p.m., adopt same procedure, you are authorized to transmit to the Chinese
                    Foreign Office the commissions of the American consular officers mentioned in
                    your 2462, December 5, and to request exequaturs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
